From b7a98d1d2b433531ef6792ac557d8cd1a748ddc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Hutsaliuk <artemgutsaliukv@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 23:03:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 152/194] pinctrl: qcom: sm7150-lpass-lpi: fix swr_tx_data mux
 value on GPIO1

The SoundWire TX data line on LPI GPIO1 answers to the third mux value,
not the first. The vendor device tree programs func3 for this signal on
GPIO1, while using func2 for the same signal on GPIO2 - the position in
LPI_PINGROUP() is the mux value written to the hardware, so listing
swr_tx_data first makes the driver select 1 where the hardware expects 3.

With the wrong value the data line never reaches the bus: the TX
SoundWire controller reports "SWR bus clsh detected" on every boot and
the TX side of the WCD9375 stays UNATTACHED, while the RX side comes up
normally.

Tested on a Xiaomi Mi 9T (SM7150-AA, WCD9375): with this change both
SoundWire buses attach, no clashes are reported, and capture works.

Signed-off-by: Artem Hutsaliuk <artemgutsaliukv@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
index a8ff049d0..0b268ac08 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -81,6 +81,13 @@ static const char * const swr_tx_data_groups[] = { "gpio1", "gpio2", "gpio5" };
 
 static const struct lpi_pingroup sm7150_groups[] = {
 	LPI_PINGROUP(0, 0, slimbus_clk, swr_tx_clk, _, _),
+	/*
+	 * The SoundWire TX data line on this pin answers to the third mux
+	 * value, not the first: the vendor tree programs func3 here while it
+	 * uses func2 for the same signal on the neighbouring pin. Selecting the
+	 * first slot leaves the line off the bus, and the controller reports a
+	 * bus clash while the TX side of the codec never enumerates.
+	 */
 	LPI_PINGROUP(1, 2, _, audio_ref, swr_tx_data, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(2, 4, slimbus_data, swr_tx_data, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(3, 8, slimbus_data, swr_rx_clk, _, _),
